# Testing requirements

- Tests should prove behavior rather than implementation trivia.
- Add regression coverage for bug fixes when practical.
- Never change an assertion solely because new code made an old test fail; first determine whether product behavior or implementation is wrong.
- Prefer the narrowest reliable test level that proves behavior while preserving end-to-end coverage for critical journeys.
- Do not mock the unit under test.
- Fix sources of nondeterminism instead of blindly increasing retries/timeouts.
- Explicitly report tests that could not be run and why.
